==English==

===Etymology===
Named after [[w:Hans Asperger|Hans Asperger]] + ''[[syndrome]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈæs.pɜː.dʒɜz ˈsɪn.dɹəʊm/}}
* {{audio|en-uk-Asperger's syndrome.ogg|Audio (UK)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|sg=Asperger’s [[syndrome]]|-}}  (''abbreviation'' '''[[AS]]''')

# {{neurology}} A high-function form  of [[Autism]], characterised by severe and sustained impairment in [[social]] [[interaction]] and [[communication]].  It is also characterised by restricted, repetitive, stereotyped activities, interests and routines.

====Translations====
{{trans-top|high-function form  of Autism}}
